face that passes through the point where $(x,y,z)=(1,-1,-1).$" 13194139534962 true] [17592186322808 1000 #edb/ref 17592186322809 13194139534962 true] [17592186322808 1000 #edb/ref 17592186322810 13194139534962 true] [17592186322808 1000 #edb/ref 17592186322811 13194139534962 true] [17592186322808 1000 #edb/ref 17592186322812 13194139534962 true] [17592186322808 1000 #edb/ref 17592186322813 13194139534962 true] [17592186322808 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534962 true] [17592186322808 1041 "selection" 13194139534962 true] [17592186322808 1104 #edb/ref 17592186322811 13194139534962 true] [17592186322808 1110 #uuid "bb02f697-86e9-5804-abbd-791fbc7667f5" 13194139534962 true] [17592186322809 1034 "3\\,i+j+k" 13194139534962 true] [17592186322809 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534962 true] [17592186322809 1111 #uuid "02751068-ad51-5264-a97f-ed1d0ab4ebf6" 13194139534962 true] [17592186322810 1034 "j-k" 13194139534962 true] [17592186322810 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534962 true] [17592186322810 1111 #uuid "bc802774-0b8b-589e-9209-b8912f2943d3" 13194139534962 true] [17592186322811 1034 "3\\,i-2\\,j" 13194139534962 true] [17592186322811 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534962 true] [17592186322811 1111 #uuid "a598ecbe-78d2-55ba-b3c7-550be513ff8c" 13194139534962 true] [17592186322812 1034 "2\\,i-2\\,j-k" 13194139534962 true] [17592186322812 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534962 true] [17592186322812 1111 #uuid "240eb88e-c808-5b31-86d3-255676d89869" 13194139534962 true] [17592186322813 1034 "-2\\,i+k" 13194139534962 true] [17592186322813 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534962 true] [17592186322813 1111 #uuid "00057f83-bb13-5625-8e40-bb4d96a6f0bb" 13194139534962 true] [17592186322814 1017 #edb/ref 17592186322815 13194139534962 true] [17592186322814 1089 "q-131126" 13194139534962 true] [17592186322814 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534962 true] [17592186322814 1100 "Find a vector equation of the normal line to the surface ${x}^{2}y+{y}^{2}z+{z}^{2}x=5$ at the point $(1,-1,2).$" 13194139534962 true] [17592186322814 1113 #uuid "aeaadd89-dc14-54c2-bff3-8d905f0aebc2" 13194139534962 true] [17592186322814 1145 "Let's set $f(x,y,z)={x}^{2}y+{y}^{2}z+{z}^{2}x.$ Then, our surface can be viewed as the level surface $f(x,y,z)=5.$ \n\nA normal vector to the level surface that passes through the point $(1,-1,2)$ can be found by computing $∇f(1,-1,2).$ \n\nSo, we find the gradient and evaluate it at $(1,-1,2):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y,z) & ={f}_{x}(x,y,z)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y,z)\\text{ }j+{f}_{z}(x,y,z)\\text{ }k \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}y+{y}^{2}z+{z}^{2}x)i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}y+{y}^{2}z+{z}^{2}x)j+\\frac{∂}{∂z}({x}^{2}y+{y}^{2}z+{z}^{2}x)k \\\\  & =(2xy+{z}^{2})\\,i+({x}^{2}+2yz)\\,j+({y}^{2}+2zx)\\,k \\\\ ∇f(1,-1,2) & =(2(1)(-1)+(2)^{2})\\text{ }i+((1)^{2}+2(-1)(2))\\text{ }j+((-1)^{2}+2(2)(1))\\text{ }k \\\\  & =2\\,i-3\\,j+5\\,k \\\\  & =⟨2,-3,5⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the vector equation of the line that is parallel to $∇f(1,-1,2)$ and passes through the point $(1,-1,2)$ can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =⟨1,-1,2⟩+t\\,∇f(1,-1,2)=⟨1,-1,2⟩+t\\,⟨2,-3,5⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$" 13194139534962 true] [17592186322815 1000 #edb/ref 17592186322816 13194139534962 true] [17592186322815 1000 #edb/ref 17592186322817 13194139534962 true] [17592186322815 1000 #edb/ref 17592186322818 13194139534962 true] [17592186322815 1000 #edb/ref 17592186322819 13194139534962 true] [17592186322815 1000 #edb/ref 17592186322820 13194139534962 true] [17592186322815 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534962 true] [17592186322815 1041 "selection" 13194139534962 true] [17592186322815 1104 #edb/ref 17592186322819 13194139534962 true] [17592186322815 1110 #uuid "225ef13f-bb07-530a-98c0-5c877c04cd97" 13194139534962 true] [17592186322816 1034 "⟨1,-1,2⟩+t\\,⟨4,5,-5⟩,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" 13194139534962 true] [17592186322816 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534962 true] [