,-1,1)$ can be found by computing $∇f(2,-1,1).$ \n\nSo, we find the gradient and evaluate it at $(2,-1,1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y,z) & ={f}_{x}(x,y,z)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y,z)\\text{ }j+{f}_{z}(x,y,z)\\text{ }k \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}yz)i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}yz)j+\\frac{∂}{∂z}({x}^{2}yz)k \\\\  & =2xyz\\text{ }i+{x}^{2}z\\text{ }j+{x}^{2}y\\,k \\\\ ∇f(2,-1,1) & =2(2)(-1)(1)\\text{ }i+(2)^{2}(1)\\text{ }j+(2)^{2}(-1)\\text{ }k \\\\  & =-4\\,i+4\\,j-4\\,k \\\\  & =⟨-4,4,-4⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the Cartesian equation of the line that is parallel to $v=⟨{v}_{x},{v}_{y},{v}_{z}⟩$ and passes through the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ can be written as:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x-{x}_{0}}{{v}_{x}}=\\frac{y-{y}_{0}}{{v}_{y}}=\\frac{z-{z}_{0}}{{v}_{z}} \\\\ \\frac{x-2}{(-4)}=\\frac{y-(-1)}{4}=\\frac{z-1}{(-4)} \\\\ \\frac{x-2}{(-1)}=\\frac{y+1}{1}=\\frac{z-1}{(-1)} \\\\ 2-x=y+1=1-z\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534962 true] [17592186322829 1000 #edb/ref 17592186322830 13194139534962 true] [17592186322829 1000 #edb/ref 17592186322831 13194139534962 true] [17592186322829 1000 #edb/ref 17592186322832 13194139534962 true] [17592186322829 1000 #edb/ref 17592186322833 13194139534962 true] [17592186322829 1000 #edb/ref 17592186322834 13194139534962 true] [17592186322829 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534962 true] [17592186322829 1041 "selection" 13194139534962 true] [17592186322829 1104 #edb/ref 17592186322831 13194139534962 true] [17592186322829 1110 #uuid "549aa6f0-0020-509b-8885-63b47ef790e2" 13194139534962 true] [17592186322830 1034 "x-2=\\frac{y+1}{2}=\\frac{z-1}{3}" 13194139534962 true] [17592186322830 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534962 true] [17592186322830 1111 #uuid "00c8ec18-b87f-5885-aa14-432139f277b6" 13194139534962 true] [17592186322831 1034 "2-x=y+1=1-z" 13194139534962 true] [17592186322831 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534962 true] [17592186322831 1111 #uuid "cc835021-dea2-5a65-82ec-0221f2a80e24" 13194139534962 true] [17