alize $∇f(0,0):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∇f(0,0)}{‖∇f(0,0)‖} & =\\frac{2i+2j}{\\sqrt{(2)^{2}+(2)^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2i+2j}{2\\sqrt{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}(i+j)\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534962 true] [17592186322878 1000 #edb/ref 17592186322879 13194139534962 true] [17592186322878 1000 #edb/ref 17592186322880 13194139534962 true] [17592186322878 1000 #edb/ref 17592186322881 13194139534962 true] [17592186322878 1000 #edb/ref 17592186322882 13194139534962 true] [17592186322878 1000 #edb/ref 17592186322883 13194139534962 true] [17592186322878 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534962 true] [17592186322878 1041 "selection" 13194139534962 true] [17592186322878 1104 #edb/ref 17592186322881 13194139534962 true] [17592186322878 1110 #uuid "7862f7d6-5bab-559c-805c-5d9bfd1fb8bc" 13194139534962 true] [17592186322879 1034 "i" 13194139534962 true] [17592186322879 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534962 true] [17592186322879 1111 #uuid "f1d89805-37e1-5010-ace2-e1d14950134c" 13194139534962 true] [17592186322880 1034 "\\frac{1}{2}(i-j)" 13194139534962 true] [17592186322880 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534962 true] [17592186322880 1111 #uuid "6a14d68d-0419-5d63-a147-890caadd27f2" 13194139534962 true] [17592186322881 1034 "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}(i+j)" 13194139534962 true] [17592186322881 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534962 true] [17592186322881 1111 #uuid "c064d1d2-4af5-5177-8d42-dc0519437209" 13194139534962 true] [17592186322882 1034 "j" 13194139534962 true] [17592186322882 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534962 true] [17592186322882 1111 #uuid "6d32b96f-3d87-509b-bdc5-aba4a32f34b2" 13194139534962 true] [17592186322883 1034 "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}(i-j)" 13194139534962 true] [17592186322883 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534962 true] [17592186322883 1111 #uuid "cd6a792f-55d4-52de-a9ea-9179d7f9c8aa" 13194139534962 true] [17592186322884 1017 #edb/ref 17592186322885 13194139534962 true] [17592186322884 1089 "q-71385" 13194139534962 true] [17592186322884 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534962 true] [17592186322884 1100 "Consider the plane curve ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=4.$  Find the equation of the normal line to the curve at the point $(2,0).$" 13194139534962 true] [17592186322884 1113 #uuid "c79c3b6c-2eb8-5187-a6a7-dda99f1e32a9" 13194139534962 true] [17592186322884 1145 "If we set $f(x,y)={x}^{2}+{y}^{2}$, our curve can be viewed as the level curve $f(x,y)=4.$  \n\nA normal vector to the level curve that passes through the point $(2,0)$ can be found by computing $∇f(2,0).$ \n\nSo, we find the gradient and evaluate it at $(2,0):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y) & ={f}_{x}(x,y)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y)\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\,i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\,j \\\\  & =2x\\,i+2y\\,j \\\\ ∇f(2,0) & =2(2)\\,i+2(0)\\,j \\\\  & =4\\,i \\\\  & =⟨4,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $∇f(2,0)=⟨4,0⟩$ is a normal vector to the curve at $(2,0).$\n\nFinally, the Cartesian equation of the line that is parallel to $v=⟨{v}_{x},{v}_{y}⟩$ and passes through the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0})$ can be written as:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-{x}_{0}){v}_{y}-(y-{y}_{0}){v}_{x} & =0 \\\\ (x-2)0-(y-0)4 & =0 \\\\ -4y & =0 \\\\ y & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534962 true] [17592186322885 1000 #edb/ref 17592186322886 13194139534962 true] [17592186322885 1000 #edb/ref 17592186322887 13194139534962 true] [17592186322885 1000 #edb/ref 17592186322888 13194139534962 true] [17592186322885 1000 #edb/ref 17592186322889 13194139534962 true] [17592186322885 1000 #edb/ref 17592186322890 13194139534962 true] [17592186322885 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534962 true] [17592186322885 1041 "selection" 13194139534962 true] [17592186322885 1104 #edb/ref 17592186322889 13194139534962 true] [17592186322885 1110 #uuid "7aac0396-8461-53ef-95c9-6222dc99a8eb" 13194139534962 true] [17592186322886 1034 "x+y=2" 13194139534962 true] [17592186322886 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534962 true] [17592186322886 1111 #uuid "02b6406b-986a-5fa0-bda7-c5bf77f5124d" 13194139534962 true] [17592186322887 1034 "x=2" 13194139534962 true] [17592186322887 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534962 true] [17592186322887 1111 #uuid "71982151-0955-55d2-8dd6-21bff01e173e" 13194139534962 true] [17592186322888 1034 "x=0" 13194139534962 true] [17592186322888 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534962 true] [17592186322888 1111 #uuid "c0497a00-5e77-52cf-8a43-fa9f6f8d08d9" 13194139534962 true] [17592186322889 1034 "y=0" 13194139534962 true] [17592186322889 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534962 true] [17592186322889 1111 #uuid "7e0f0ad2-f181-5207-8f0a-23526349efd9" 13194139534962 true] [17592186322890 1034 "x-y=2" 13194139534962 true] [17592186322890 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534962 true] [17592186322890 1111 #uuid "facad33b-6fa8-53c5-9b07-bcacded2a777" 13194139534962 true] [17592186322891 1017 #edb/ref 17592186322892 13194139534962 true] [17592186322891 1089 "q-71393" 13194139534962 true] [17592186322891 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534962 true] [17592186322891 1100 "Consider the plane curve $\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+y)=2xy.$  Find the equation of the normal line to the curve at the point $(0,1).$" 13194139534962 true] [17592186322891 1113 #uuid "4e876b2a-993c-5d99-82f5-7108f1c93929" 13194139534962 true] [17592186322891 1145 "First, we bring all variables to one side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+y) & =2xy \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+y)-2xy & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we set $f(x,y)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+y)-2xy$, our curve can be viewed as the level curve $f(x,y)=0.$  \n\nA normal vector to the level curve that passes through the point $(0,1)$ can be found by computing $∇f(0,1).$ \n\nSo, we find the gradient and evaluate it at $(0,1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y) & ={f}_{x}(x,y)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y)\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+y)-2xy)\\,i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+y)-2xy)\\,j \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{x+y}-2y)\\,i+(\\frac{1}{x+y}-2x)\\,j \\\\ ∇f(0,1) & =(\\frac{1}{0+1}-2(1))\\,i+(\\frac{1}{0+1}-2(0))\\,j \\\\  & =-i+j \\\\  & =⟨-1,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $∇f(0,1)=⟨-1,1⟩$ is a normal vector to the curve at $(0,1).$\n\nFinally, the Cartesian equation of the line that is parallel to $v=⟨{v}_{x},{v}_{y}⟩$ and passes through the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0})$ can be written as:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x-{x}_{0}}{{v}_{x}} & =\\frac{y-{y}_{0}}{{v}_{y}} \\\\ \\frac{x-0}{-1} & =\\frac{y-1}{1} \\\\ -x & =y-1 \\\\ x+y-1 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534962 true] [17592186322892 1000 #edb/ref 17592186322893 13194139534962 true] [17592186322892 1000 #edb/ref 17592186322894 13194139534962 true] [17592186322892 1000 #edb/ref 17592186322895 13194139534962 true] [17592186322892 1000 #edb/ref 17592186322896 13194139534962 true] [17592186322892 1000 #edb/ref 17592186322897 13194139534962 true] [17592186322892 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534962 true] [17592186322892 1041 "selection" 13194139534962 true] [17592186322892 1104 #edb/ref 17592186322895 13194139534962 true] [17592186322892 1110 #uuid "bb18e819-5242-5710-986b-75ec6fb8fe7e" 13194139534962 true] [17592186322893 1034 "-x+y-1=0" 13194139534962 true] [17592186322893 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534962 true] [17592186322893 1111 #uuid "0e3c6c1d-ae7a-50f0-970e-12603e07e9db" 13194139534962 true] [17592186322894 1034 "x+y+1=0" 13194139534962 true] [17592186322894 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534962 true] [17592186322894 1111 #uuid "18d09da2-9bce-56c8-a1a4-55b504f62940" 13194139534962 true] [17592186322895 1034 "x+y-1=0" 13194139534962 true] [17592186322895 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534962 true] [17592186322895 1111 #uuid "df01a1e5-2f92-5dbf-93b6-07ba00c5251b" 13194139534962 true] [17592186322896 1034 "x+2y-2=0" 13194139534962 true] [17592186322896 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534962 true] [17592186322896 1111 #uuid "89dd655b-7b38-5bd8-81de-533157f67d36" 13194139534962 true] [17592186322897 1034 "x-y+1=0" 13194139534962 true] [1759218632